          <div class="mistake-item__title">{item.title}</div>
          <p>{item.body}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <p>
    If you already have proof and a targeted list of roles but are still not converting to interviews, the gap
    is usually positioning, not the underlying ability. A session with
    <a href="https://futurecareerschool.com/services/career-counselling-and-career-guidance/">career guidance</a>
    can help pinpoint what is actually costing you shortlists — the same guidance that helps you choose a
    high-income skill portfolio worth building in the first place, not just fix one resume. Or start with the
    free <a href="https://futurecareerschool.com/services/assessments">career and skill assessments</a> if you
    are still unsure which roles genuinely fit how you like to work.
  </p>

  <h2 id="first-90-days">Your first 90 days once you land the job</h2>

  <p>
    Getting hired is not the finish line. The way you use your first 90 days decides whether this job stays a
    single line on a resume or becomes the next real entry in a growing skill portfolio, one that eventually
    unlocks better-paying roles instead of another no-experience search a year from now.
  </p>

  <div class="mistakes-list">
    {first90DaysItems.map((item) => (
