          <p>{item.body}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <h2 id="sources">Check the sources behind these claims</h2>

  <p>Do not trust any single career article blindly, including this one. Check the primary sources and apply your own judgment.</p>
  <ul class="sources">
    <li>
      Volunteer work valued equally to paid experience by hiring managers, and broader skill-building impact of volunteering.
      <a href="https://www.finalroundai.com/blog/volunteering-work-experience" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Final Round AI: Volunteering as Work Experience</a>
    </li>
    <li>
      Proof-of-work artifacts, cold outreach conversion, and translating prior experience for career changers.
      <a href="https://aiapplyd.com/blog/career-change-no-experience" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AI Applyd: Career Change With No Experience</a>
    </li>
    <li>
      Structured career-change strategy: transferable skills, referrals, and unpaid or volunteer entry points into a new field.
      <a href="https://www.careershifters.org/expert-advice/how-to-move-into-a-new-career-with-no-relevant-experience" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Careershifters: Moving Into a New Career With No Relevant Experience</a>
    </li>
    <li>
      India's gig and platform-based workforce growth projections through 2030.
      <a href="https://www.ibef.org/blogs/emergence-of-india-s-gig-economy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IBEF: Emergence of India's Gig Economy</a>
    </li>
    <li>
      India Skills Report 2026 on skills-first hiring, gig work, freelancing, and rising employer hiring intent.
      <a href="https://pmwares.com/the-india-skills-report-2026-the-future-of-work/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">India Skills Report 2026: The Future of Work</a>
    </li>
    <li>
      Referral hiring share and the role of employee referral programs in filling open roles.
      <a href="https://www.indeed.com/career-advice/finding-a-job/career-change-jobs-with-no-experience" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Indeed: Career Change Jobs With No Experience</a>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="faq">FAQs on how to get a job without experience in India</h2>

  <div class="faq-accordion">
    {faqItems.map((item, index) => (
      <details open={index === 0}>
        <summary>{item.q}</summary>
        <div class="faq-a">{item.a}</div>
      </details>
    ))}
  </div>

  <p>
    The experience requirement on most entry-level postings is a filter, not a locked door. Widen what counts
    as proof, describe it with the same structure a job entry would use, aim at employers actually built to
    train people from zero, and get useful to someone before you ask to be paid. That combination is what
    actually moves a no-experience application from ignored to interviewed.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>Do not stop at closing this one gap.</strong> Each project, gig, apprenticeship, or portfolio piece
    you build to solve it becomes part of a high-income skill portfolio you carry into every job after this one
    — which is the difference between one lucky break and a path toward earlier financial freedom.
  </p>

